IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `poa-dates`
IMPORT `poa-core`

-- Powers of Attorney Act 1998 (Qld) -- claims about an attorney's dealings, from the seat of the attorney answering them.
--
-- SEAT: the attorney: a person appointed under a power of attorney, an enduring power of attorney or an advance health
-- directive (or a statutory health attorney), against whom a principal, their estate or a beneficiary brings a claim.
-- "Was I allowed to do this? Am I protected because I followed the court's advice, or did not know the power was
-- invalid? Can the court relieve me? What can I be ordered to pay? Must I keep my property separate? Can I resign? What
-- can I be fined?" The rules are in poa-core.l4, shared with the claimant's seat (poa-seat.l4) so the two cannot
-- disagree; this module restates no rule and defines no name the claimant's seat defines.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Powers of Attorney Act 1998 (Qld) -- the attorney's questions`

DECLARE `Fine answer` IS ONE OF
    `the most you can be fined is, in penalty units` HAS `penalty units` IS A NUMBER
    `the Act does not settle this: ss 26, 61, 66, 71, 74A and 86 do not make that conduct an offence (other law may)`

§§ `What I was allowed to do (ss 73, 86)`

@export As attorney, was I allowed to enter into this transaction, given a possible conflict of interest?
GIVEN `what the transaction could conflict with` IS A `Conflict` @desc What your duty to the principal could conflict with in the transaction: your own interests; the interests of your relation, business associate or close friend; another duty of yours; or nothing
      `where the conflict comes from` IS A `Source of the conflict` @desc Where the conflict comes from: merely that you are related to the principal; merely that you may inherit from the principal; merely a dealing with property you and the principal hold or acquire jointly (or a loan or guarantee for it); the transaction is a gift under s 88; it provides for the principal's dependant under s 89; or something else
      `who authorised it` IS AN `Authorisation` @desc Who authorised it: the principal, beforehand (this transaction, its type, or conflict transactions generally); the court, beforehand; the principal, afterwards, while they had capacity; the court, afterwards; or nobody
GIVETH A `Conflict answer`
DECIDE `As attorney, was I allowed to enter into this transaction` IS
    `the s 73 answer` `what the transaction could conflict with` `where the conflict comes from` `who authorised it`

@export As attorney under an enduring power of attorney, must I keep my own property separate from the principal's?
GIVEN `the kind of attorney I am` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document you act under: a general power of attorney made under the Act; an enduring power of attorney; an advance health directive; a power of attorney made under another law; or as statutory health attorney
      `the property is owned jointly by the principal and me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the property in question is owned jointly by you and the principal
      `we bought it jointly to replace jointly owned property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the principal acquired it jointly in place of property you owned jointly
GIVETH A `Separate property answer`
DECIDE `Must I keep my property separate from the principal's` IS
    `the s 86 answer` `the kind of attorney I am` `the property is owned jointly by the principal and me` `we bought it jointly to replace jointly owned property`

§§ `Protection and relief (ss 97, 98, 105)`

@export As attorney, am I taken to have complied with the Act because I followed the court's advice or directions?
GIVEN `I followed the court's advice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you acted in compliance with the Supreme Court's (or QCAT's) advice, directions or recommendations
      `I knowingly gave the court false or misleading information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you knowingly gave the court false or misleading information relevant to that advice
GIVETH A `Court advice answer`
DECIDE `Am I protected because I followed the court's advice` IS
    `the s 97 answer` `I followed the court's advice` `I knowingly gave the court false or misleading information`

@export As attorney, am I liable because the power I used turned out to be invalid?
GIVEN `the kind of attorney I am` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document you act under (see the separate property question)
      `why the power was invalid` IS AN `Invalidity` @desc Why the power was invalid when you used it: the document was made in another jurisdiction and does not comply with its requirements; it had been revoked (wholly or for that power); the power was not yet exercisable; or it was valid
      `I knew it was invalid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you knew the power was invalid
      `I knew of the event that made it invalid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you knew of the event that made it invalid (for example, that the principal had revoked it)
      `I had reason to believe it was invalid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had reason to believe the power was invalid
GIVETH AN `Invalid power answer`
DECIDE `Am I liable for using a power I did not know was invalid` IS
    `the s 98 answer` `the kind of attorney I am` `why the power was invalid`
        (`knew of the invalidity` `I knew it was invalid` `I knew of the event that made it invalid` `I had reason to believe it was invalid`)

@export As attorney, can the court relieve me from personal liability for a breach of the Act?
GIVEN `I am or may be personally liable for a breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, or may be, personally liable for a breach of the Act
      `the court considers I acted honestly and reasonably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court considers you acted honestly and reasonably
      `the court considers I ought fairly to be excused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court considers you ought fairly to be excused for the breach
GIVETH A `Relief answer`
DECIDE `Can the court relieve me from personal liability` IS
    `the s 105 answer` `I am or may be personally liable for a breach` `the court considers I acted honestly and reasonably` `the court considers I ought fairly to be excused`

§§ `What I can be ordered to pay or fined (ss 26, 61, 66, 71, 74A, 86, 106)`

@export As attorney, can I be ordered to pay compensation or account for my profits for not complying with the Act?
GIVEN `the kind of attorney I am` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document you act under (see the separate property question)
      `I failed to comply with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to comply with the Act when exercising a power
      `it caused the principal a loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that failure caused the principal a loss
      `I profited from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made profits as a result of that failure
      `the principal has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal has died
GIVETH A `Compensation answer`
DECIDE `Can I be ordered to pay compensation or my profits` IS
    `the s 106 answer` `the kind of attorney I am` `I failed to comply with the Act` `it caused the principal a loss` `I profited from it` `the principal has died`

@export As attorney, what is the most I can be fined for this conduct?
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `Conduct` @desc What you did: dishonestly getting someone to make or revoke a power of attorney, or an enduring document; not acting honestly and with reasonable diligence to protect the principal's interests; using a power you knew was revoked; using confidential information without authority or reasonable excuse; not keeping your property separate from the principal's; or other conduct
GIVETH A `Fine answer`
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined` IS
    IF `the maximum penalty in penalty units` `what I did` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the most you can be fined is, in penalty units` (`the maximum penalty in penalty units` `what I did`)
    ELSE `the Act does not settle this: ss 26, 61, 66, 71, 74A and 86 do not make that conduct an offence (other law may)`

§§ `Resigning (ss 72, 82)`

@export As attorney, can I resign?
GIVEN `the kind of attorney I am` IS A `Kind of attorney` @desc The kind of document you act under (see the separate property question)
      `the principal can understand decisions about the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal is now capable of understanding the nature and effect of decisions about the matter
      `the principal can make decisions freely and voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal is now capable of freely and voluntarily making decisions about the matter
      `the principal can communicate decisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the principal is now capable of communicating decisions in some way
      `the court has given me leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court (or QCAT) has given you leave to resign
GIVETH A `Resignation answer`
DECIDE `Can I resign as attorney` IS
    `the resignation answer` `the kind of attorney I am`
        (NOT (`has capacity for the matter` `the principal can understand decisions about the matter` `the principal can make decisions freely and voluntarily` `the principal can communicate decisions`))
        `the court has given me leave`
